                    {
                        "id": "6d463f91-6e6b-4694-b42c-cb57df32fb3c",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "People get energy and nutrients primarily through eating healthy food (option D). However, it is essential to understand the different aspects of how the body obtains and utilizes energy and nutrients.\n\nHelpful knowledge and important additional facts:\n1. Energy and nutrients are essential for the body to function properly.\n2. Energy is required for various bodily functions, such as maintaining body temperature, contracting muscles, and carrying out metabolic processes.\n3. Nutrients are substances that the body needs to grow, repair itself, and function properly. They include carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins, minerals, and water.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. How does the body obtain energy from food?\n2. What are the different types of nutrients, and how do they contribute to the body's functioning?\n3. How do other factors, such as breathing clean air, exercising, and getting plenty of rest, contribute to overall health and well-being?\n\nAnswers to sub-questions:\n1. The body obtains energy from food through the process of digestion. During digestion, food is broken down into its constituent nutrients, which are then absorbed into the bloodstream and transported to cells throughout the body. The cells use these nutrients to produce energy in the form of adenosine triphosphate (ATP), which powers various cellular processes.\n\n2. The different types of nutrients and their contributions to the body's functioning are as follows:\n   a. Carbohydrates: These are the body's primary source of energy. They are broken down into glucose, which is used to produce ATP.\n   b. Proteins: These are essential for growth, repair, and maintenance of body tissues. They also play a role in the production of enzymes, hormones, and other important molecules.\n   c. Fats: These are a concentrated source of energy and are essential for the absorption of fat-soluble vitamins. They also provide insulation and protection for vital organs.\n   d. Vitamins: These are organic compounds that the body needs in small amounts to support various functions, such as immune system function, bone health, and energy production.\n   e. Minerals: These are inorganic substances that the body needs for various functions, such as maintaining fluid balance, nerve function, and muscle contraction.\n   f. Water: This is essential for maintaining hydration, regulating body temperature, and transporting nutrients and waste products.\n\n3. Breathing clean air (option A), exercising and playing (option B), and getting plenty of rest (option C) contribute to overall health and well-being but do not directly provide energy and nutrients.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "8250d904-2e01-427d-a455-11777577c406",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) eating healthy food. This is the primary way people obtain energy and nutrients, which are essential for the body to function properly. Other factors, such as breathing clean air, exercising, and getting plenty of rest, contribute to overall health and well-being but do not directly provide energy and nutrients.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
