                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\n1. First, let's define what a first-level consumer is. A first-level consumer is an organism that eats producers, which are plants or other autotrophic organisms that produce their own food through photosynthesis.\n\n2. Looking at the options, we can eliminate A) wolf and B) hawk because they are both predators that eat other animals, making them second-level consumers or higher.\n\n3. Option C) carrot is a producer, not a consumer, so it cannot be a first-level consumer.\n\n4. This leaves us with option D) rabbit. Rabbits are herbivores that eat plants, making them first-level consumers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) rabbit.",
