                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine the best tool for Jessica to use to see the cells in an oak tree leaf, we need to consider the size of the cells and the magnification capabilities of each tool.\n\nA) Binoculars are designed for viewing distant objects and typically have a magnification of around 7x to 10x. They are not suitable for viewing small objects like cells up close.\n\nB) Microscopes are specifically designed for viewing small objects at high magnification. They can magnify objects up to 1000x or more, which is ideal for viewing cells.\n\nC) Reading glasses are designed to help people with difficulty focusing on close-up objects, but they do not provide significant magnification. They are not suitable for viewing cells.\n\nD) Magnifying glasses can provide some magnification, typically around 2x to 10x, but this is not enough to clearly see the details of cells.\n\nBased on the magnification capabilities of each tool, the best option for Jessica to use to see the cells in an oak tree leaf is:\n\nB) microscope",
