                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: Which tool is the most suitable for Jessica to use in order to observe the cells in an oak tree leaf?\nOptions:\nA) binoculars\nB) microscope\nC) reading glasses\nD) magnifying glass\n\nStep 1: Understand the purpose of each tool.\nA) Binoculars are used for viewing distant objects.\nB) Microscopes are used for observing small objects or details that are not visible to the naked eye.\nC) Reading glasses are used for improving vision while reading or doing close-up work.\nD) Magnifying glasses are used for enlarging small objects or details, but not to the extent of a microscope.\n\nStep 2: Determine which tool is most appropriate for observing cells.\nCells are microscopic structures that cannot be seen with the naked eye. Therefore, a tool that can magnify objects to a high degree is necessary.\n\nStep 3: Compare the tools and select the best option.\nA) Binoculars are not suitable for observing cells, as they are designed for viewing distant objects.\nB) Microscopes are specifically designed for observing small objects or details, making them the most suitable option for viewing cells.\nC) Reading glasses may help with close-up work, but they do not provide enough magnification to observe cells.\nD) Magnifying glasses can enlarge small objects or details, but they do not provide the level of magnification necessary to observe cells.\n\nAnswer: B) Microscope",
                        "answers": [
