                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: I'm not sure which tool Jessica should use to see the cells in an oak tree leaf. Can you help me figure it out?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's go through the options one by one. First, we have binoculars. What do you think binoculars are used for?\n\nStudent: Binoculars are used for seeing things that are far away, like birds or distant objects.\n\nProfessor: That's correct. So, do you think binoculars would be helpful for seeing cells in a leaf?\n\nStudent: No, I don't think so. Cells are really small, and binoculars wouldn't help with that.\n\nProfessor: Good reasoning. Now, let's consider a microscope. What do you know about microscopes?\n\nStudent: Microscopes are used to see really small things, like cells and bacteria.\n\nProfessor: Exactly. So, do you think a microscope would be a good tool for Jessica to use?\n\nStudent: Yes, I think a microscope would be the best tool for her to use.\n\nProfessor: Great! Let's quickly go through the other options just to make sure. What about reading glasses?\n\nStudent: Reading glasses are used to help people see things up close, like when they're reading a book. But I don't think they would be strong enough to see cells in a leaf.\n\nProfessor: Correct. And finally, what about a magnifying glass?\n\nStudent: A magnifying glass can make things look bigger, but I don't think it would be powerful enough to see cells in a leaf.\n\nProfessor: You're right. So, based on our discussion, which tool do you think is the best for Jessica to use to see the cells in an oak tree leaf?\n\nStudent: I think the best tool for Jessica to use is a microscope.\n\nProfessor: Excellent! You've worked through the options and arrived at the correct answer. Well done!",
