                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the terms\n- Element: A pure substance that cannot be broken down into simpler substances by chemical means. Examples include hydrogen, oxygen, and iron.\n- Mixture: A combination of two or more substances that are not chemically combined and can be separated by physical means. Examples include salt and sand, or oil and water.\n- Solution: A homogeneous mixture of two or more substances, where one substance is dissolved in another. Examples include saltwater or sugar dissolved in water.\n- Compound: A substance made up of two or more elements that are chemically combined in fixed proportions. Examples include water (H2O) and carbon dioxide (CO2).\n\nStep 2: Analyze the given information\nIron oxide is formed when iron chemically combines with oxygen. This means that iron and oxygen are chemically bonded together in fixed proportions.\n\nStep 3: Match the information with the correct term\nSince iron oxide is made up of two elements (iron and oxygen) that are chemically combined in fixed proportions, it best fits the definition of a compound.\n\nAnswer: D) compound",
