                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking in which aspect protons and electrons are always equal. We need to compare the given options and determine which one is true for both protons and electrons.\n\nStep 2: Analyze each option\nA) Mass number: The mass number is the total number of protons and neutrons in an atom. Protons and electrons are subatomic particles, not atoms, so this option is not relevant.\n\nB) Kinetic energy: Kinetic energy depends on the mass and velocity of a particle. Protons and electrons have different masses and can have different velocities, so their kinetic energies are not always equal.\n\nC) Sign of charge: Protons have a positive charge, while electrons have a negative charge. Their charges have opposite signs, so this option is not correct.\n\nD) Magnitude of charge: The magnitude of charge refers to the absolute value of the charge of a particle, without considering its sign. Protons have a charge of +1 elementary charge, and electrons have a charge of -1 elementary charge. The magnitudes of their charges are equal, both being 1 elementary charge.\n\nStep 3: Choose the correct answer\nThe correct answer is D) magnitude of charge, as protons and electrons always have equal magnitudes of charge, both being 1 elementary charge.",
                        "answers": [
