                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, let's first understand the properties of protons and electrons.\n\nProtons are positively charged particles found in the nucleus of an atom. They have a mass of approximately 1 atomic mass unit (amu).\n\nElectrons are negatively charged particles that orbit the nucleus of an atom. They have a much smaller mass, approximately 1/1836 amu.\n\nNow let's analyze each option:\n\nA) Mass number: This refers to the total number of protons and neutrons in an atom. Since electrons have a much smaller mass than protons, they do not contribute significantly to the mass number. Therefore, protons and electrons are not equal in this respect.\n\nB) Kinetic energy: This is the energy possessed by an object due to its motion. The kinetic energy of protons and electrons can vary depending on their speed and mass. Therefore, they are not always equal in this respect.\n\nC) Sign of charge: Protons have a positive charge, while electrons have a negative charge. The sign of their charges is opposite, so they are not equal in this respect.\n\nD) Magnitude of charge: The magnitude of charge refers to the absolute value of the charge, without considering its sign. Both protons and electrons have a charge of approximately 1.6 x 10^-19 coulombs. The magnitudes of their charges are equal, even though their signs are opposite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) magnitude of charge. Protons and electrons are always equal in the magnitude of their charge.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "ffdd4027-29b3-4f4d-a9c6-e88d269bac3b",
