                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "How can we describe the reason why an ice cube melts when set out in a warm room?\n\nLet's break down the answer choices:\n\nA) Heat from the room is absorbed by the ice cube.\nThis is a possible reason why the ice cube melts. When the ice cube is exposed to a warmer environment, heat energy is transferred from the room to the ice cube, causing it to melt.\n\nB) The ice cube molecules move more slowly.\nThis is not a correct reason why the ice cube melts. When the ice cube is exposed to a warmer environment, the ice molecules actually move faster, causing the ice to melt.\n\nC) One side of the ice cube is colder than the other.\nThis is not a correct reason why the ice cube melts. The temperature of the ice cube is uniform throughout, and it is the warmer temperature of the room that causes the ice to melt.\n\nD) Heat from the ice cube moves into the air.\nThis is not a correct reason why the ice cube melts. The heat energy is actually transferred from the room to the ice cube, causing it to melt.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) Heat from the room is absorbed by the ice cube.",
