                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's rephrase the question: What is the explanation for an ice cube melting when it is placed in a warm room?\n\nNow, let's work this out step by step:\n\n1. An ice cube is a solid form of water, and it melts when it turns into a liquid form.\n2. For this phase change to occur, the temperature of the ice cube must increase.\n3. Heat transfer is the process by which the temperature of an object increases or decreases.\n4. In this case, the warm room has a higher temperature than the ice cube, so heat will transfer from the room to the ice cube.\n5. As the ice cube absorbs heat, its temperature increases, causing the molecules to move faster and eventually change from a solid to a liquid state.\n\nBased on our reasoning, the correct answer is:\n\nA) Heat from the room is absorbed by the ice cube.",
