                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, let's first define each term:\n\nA) Solute: A substance that is dissolved in a solvent to form a solution.\nB) Solvent: A substance that dissolves a solute to form a solution.\nC) Solution: A homogeneous mixture of two or more substances, where one substance (the solute) is dissolved in another substance (the solvent).\nD) Suspension: A heterogeneous mixture in which small particles of a substance are dispersed throughout a liquid or gas, but the particles do not dissolve.\n\nNow let's analyze the given situation:\n\nA student dissolves a spoonful of sugar in a glass of water.\n\nIn this case, sugar is the solute because it is being dissolved, and water is the solvent because it is the substance in which the sugar is being dissolved. When the sugar is completely dissolved in the water, it forms a homogeneous mixture, which is a solution. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\nC) Solution.",
