                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to understand the definitions of solute, solvent, solution, and suspension.\n\nA solute is a substance that is dissolved in a solvent to form a solution. In this case, sugar is the solute.\n\nA solvent is a substance that dissolves a solute to form a solution. In this case, water is the solvent.\n\nA solution is a homogeneous mixture of two or more substances, where one substance (the solute) is dissolved in another substance (the solvent). In this case, the sugar dissolved in water forms a solution.\n\nA suspension is a heterogeneous mixture in which particles of a substance are dispersed throughout a liquid or gas but are not dissolved. The particles eventually settle out due to gravity. In this case, the sugar is dissolved in the water, so it is not a suspension.\n\nNow we can answer the original question:\n\nA student dissolves a spoonful of sugar in a glass of water and makes a:\n\nC) solution.",
