                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: I'm not sure about the answer to this question. Can you help me understand the difference between a solute, solvent, solution, and suspension?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's start with the solute. A solute is the substance that is being dissolved in a solvent. In this case, what do you think the solute is?\n\nStudent: I think the solute is the sugar since it's being dissolved.\n\nProfessor: That's correct! Now, let's move on to the solvent. A solvent is the substance in which the solute is being dissolved. In this case, what do you think the solvent is?\n\nStudent: The solvent must be the water since the sugar is being dissolved in it.\n\nProfessor: Exactly! Now, a solution is a homogeneous mixture of two or more substances, where the solute is evenly distributed within the solvent. So, in this case, what do you think the solution is?\n\nStudent: The solution would be the mixture of sugar and water, right?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct! Finally, a suspension is a heterogeneous mixture in which the solute particles do not dissolve but remain suspended throughout the solvent. In this case, do you think we have a suspension?\n\nStudent: No, I don't think so, because the sugar dissolves completely in the water.\n\nProfessor: You're right! So, based on our discussion, what do you think the correct answer is?\n\nStudent: I think the correct answer is C) solution, since the sugar dissolves in the water to form a homogeneous mixture.\n\nProfessor: Well done! You've understood the concepts and arrived at the correct answer. Keep up the good work!",
