                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Electrical wires are used to transmit electricity from one point to another. The flow of electricity through a wire is called an electric current. \n\nAdditional facts: Rubber and plastic are both non-metallic materials commonly used as coatings for electrical wires. \n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the purpose of coating electrical wires?\n2. What are the properties of rubber and plastic that make them suitable for coating electrical wires?\n3. What are the different types of materials that can be used to coat electrical wires?\n4. What are the properties of conductors, resistors, magnets, and insulators?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The purpose of coating electrical wires is to prevent the flow of electric current from escaping the wire and causing harm to people or objects nearby. \n2. Rubber and plastic are both good insulators, meaning they do not conduct electricity well. This property makes them suitable for coating electrical wires because they prevent the flow of electric current from escaping the wire. Additionally, rubber and plastic are flexible and durable, which makes them easy to work with and long-lasting. \n3. Other materials that can be used to coat electrical wires include glass, ceramic, and metal. \n4. Conductors are materials that allow electric current to flow through them easily, while resistors are materials that impede the flow of electric current. Magnets are materials that produce a magnetic field, while insulators are materials that do not conduct electricity well and prevent the flow of electric current. \n\nAnswer: Electrical wires are coated with rubber or plastic because these materials are good insulators, meaning they prevent the flow of electric current from escaping the wire.",
                        "answers": [
