                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the purpose of coating electrical wires\nThe purpose of coating electrical wires is to prevent the flow of electricity from the wire to any other conductive material that it may come into contact with. This helps to prevent electrical shocks, short circuits, and other electrical hazards.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the given options\nWe need to determine which of the given options serves the purpose of preventing the flow of electricity.\n\nA) Resistors: Resistors are components that limit the flow of electric current in a circuit. They do not completely prevent the flow of electricity.\n\nB) Magnets: Magnets produce a magnetic field and can attract or repel certain materials, but they do not have any direct effect on the flow of electricity.\n\nC) Insulators: Insulators are materials that do not allow the flow of electric current. They are used to separate conductive materials and prevent the flow of electricity between them.\n\nD) Conductors: Conductors are materials that allow the flow of electric current. They are not suitable for coating electrical wires, as they would not prevent the flow of electricity.\n\nStep 3: Choose the correct answer\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is C) Insulators, as they prevent the flow of electric current and serve the purpose of coating electrical wires.",
