. Would a conductor be a good material to coat electrical wires with?\n\nStudent: No, because it would allow the electricity to escape the wire, which could be dangerous.\n\nProfessor: That's right. A conductor would not be a good material for a wire coating because it would allow the flow of electricity, which could be hazardous. So, option D is not the correct answer. Therefore, the correct answer is that electrical wires are coated with rubber or plastic because these materials are good ins",
