                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nReformulated Question: Why are electrical wires coated with rubber or plastic?\n\nStep by Step: \n1. Rubber and plastic are materials that can be used to coat electrical wires. \n2. We need to determine why these materials are used for this purpose. \n3. We can look at the four answer choices to determine which one best fits the purpose of coating electrical wires. \nA) Resistors: This is not the correct answer because resistors are used to control the flow of electricity, not to coat wires. \nB) Magnets: This is not the correct answer because magnets are used to create a magnetic field, not to coat wires. \nC) Insulators: This is the correct answer because insulators are materials that do not allow electricity to pass through them, which is why they are used to coat electrical wires. \nD) Conductors: This is not the correct answer because conductors are materials that allow electricity to pass through them, which is why they are not used to coat electrical wires. \n\nAnswer: C) Insulators",
