                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking us to identify a chemical property of a material.\n\nStep 2: Define chemical property\nA chemical property is a characteristic of a substance that describes how it interacts with other substances to form new substances.\n\nStep 3: Analyze the options\nA) Density: Density is a physical property that describes the amount of mass per unit volume of a substance. It does not describe how the substance interacts with other substances to form new substances. Therefore, it is not a chemical property.\n\nB) Flammability: Flammability is a chemical property that describes how easily a substance can catch fire and burn. It describes how the substance interacts with oxygen in the air to form new substances (such as carbon dioxide and water vapor). Therefore, it is a chemical property.\n\nC) Color: Color is a physical property that describes the appearance of a substance. It does not describe how the substance interacts with other substances to form new substances. Therefore, it is not a chemical property.\n\nD) Brittleness: Brittleness is a physical property that describes how easily a substance can break or shatter. It does not describe how the substance interacts with other substances to form new substances. Therefore, it is not a chemical property.\n\nStep 4: Identify the correct answer\nThe correct answer is B) flammability, as it is a chemical property that describes how a substance interacts with other substances to form new substances.",
