                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nFirst, let's look at the definition of a chemical property: \n\n\"A chemical property is a characteristic that gives a substance the ability to undergo a specific chemical reaction or produce a specific chemical product.\" \n\nFrom this definition, we can see that a chemical property must have to do with a chemical reaction. \n\nNow, let's look at each answer choice and see if it has to do with a chemical reaction: \n\nA) density - no, this does not have to do with a chemical reaction \nB) flammability - yes, this has to do with a chemical reaction because it is a characteristic that gives a substance the ability to burn \nC) color - no, this does not have to do with a chemical reaction\nD) brittleness - yes, this has to do with a chemical reaction because it is a characteristic that gives a substance the ability to break \n\nTherefore, the answer is B) flammability.",
                        "answers": [
