                        "cot": "A) The temperature of both cups will be the same. - This is unlikely because the frozen water will be at a lower temperature than the melted ice.\n\nB) Both samples in the cups will be in the same state. - This is possible because the frozen water will become ice, and the melted ice will become water.\n\nC) Both groups will have the same mass with which they started. - This is true because the mass of the water and ice will not change during the experiment.\n\nD) The time required for the changes in states of matter will be the same. - This is unlikely because the time it takes to freeze water and melt ice can vary depending on various factors.\n\nSo, the most likely outcome is C) Both groups will have the same mass with which they started.",
