                        "cot": "\n\nStudent: Professor, which of these will most likely occur at the end of the experiment?\n\nProfessor: The most likely outcome is that the group who melted the ice will have more water than the group who froze the water. This is because when you melt ice, you are essentially adding water to the cup. When you freeze water, you are essentially removing water from the cup. So, at the end of the experiment, the group with the melted ice will have more water than the group who started with frozen water.",
