                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nComplementary Knowledge: A graph is a visual representation of data, typically used to show the relationship between two or more variables. The x-axis is the horizontal axis and the y-axis is the vertical axis.\n\nSub-Questions:\n1. What is the purpose of a graph?\n2. What is the difference between the x-axis and the y-axis?\n\nAnswer to Sub-Question 1: The purpose of a graph is to show the relationship between two or more variables.\n\nAnswer to Sub-Question 2: The x-axis is the horizontal axis and typically shows the independent variable, while the y-axis is the vertical axis and typically shows the dependent variable.\n\nAnswer to Original Question:\nC) dependent variables",
                        "answers": [
